WEBVTT


00:01:24.433 --> 00:01:25.730
Wait for it.


00:01:26.669 --> 00:01:28.637
-Can l turn on the radio?
-No.


00:01:33.008 --> 00:01:35.636
Jane, you can't keep doing this.


00:01:36.645 --> 00:01:40.479
The last 1 7 occurrences
have been predictable to the second.


00:01:40.616 --> 00:01:43.084
Jane, you're an astrophysicist,
not some storm chaser.


00:01:43.185 --> 00:01:44.982
l'm telling you, there's a connection


00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.850
between these atmospheric
disturbances and my research.


00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:52.518
Erik, l wouldn't have asked you
to fly out here if l wasn't absolutely sure.


00:01:52.861 --> 00:01:53.987
Jane?


00:01:54.363 --> 00:01:55.660
l think you want to see this.


00:02:00.035 --> 00:02:01.161
What is that?


00:02:08.377 --> 00:02:11.175
l thought you said
it was a subtle aurora!


00:02:11.313 --> 00:02:12.439
Go!


00:02:19.388 --> 00:02:21.686
-Get closer.
-Right. Good one.


00:02:21.824 --> 00:02:22.848
Go!


00:02:40.743 --> 00:02:41.835
What are you doing?


00:02:41.944 --> 00:02:45.004
l am not dying for six college credits!


00:03:06.068 --> 00:03:07.933
l think that was legally your fault.


00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:09.537
Get the first aid kit.


00:03:09.738 --> 00:03:11.262
Do me a favor and don't be dead.


00:03:11.407 --> 00:03:12.669
Please.


00:03:18.113 --> 00:03:19.512
Where did he come from?


00:03:37.399 --> 00:03:39.026
<i>Once,</i>


00:03:39.134 --> 00:03:42.865
<i>mankind accepted a simple truth,</i>


00:03:42.971 --> 00:03:46.600
<i>that they were not alone</i>
<i>in this universe.</i>


00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:52.610
<i>Some worlds man believed</i>
<i>to be home to their gods.</i>


00:03:52.981 --> 00:03:55.711
<i>Others, they knew to fear.</i>


00:03:59.488 --> 00:04:04.050
<i>From a realm of cold and darkness</i>
<i>came the Frost Giants,</i>


00:04:17.773 --> 00:04:21.937
<i>threatening to plunge the mortal world</i>
<i>into a new ice age.</i>


00:04:27.816 --> 00:04:32.344
<i>But humanity</i>
<i>would not face this threat alone.</i>


00:05:08.857 --> 00:05:13.294
<i>Our armies drove the Frost Giants</i>
<i>back into the heart of their own world.</i>


00:05:16.765 --> 00:05:18.892
<i>The cost was great.</i>


00:05:19.668 --> 00:05:21.329
<i>ln the end,</i>


00:05:21.436 --> 00:05:23.631
<i>their king fell.</i>


00:05:27.843 --> 00:05:31.301
<i>And the source of their power</i>
<i>was taken from them.</i>


00:05:32.247 --> 00:05:34.477
<i>With the last great war ended,</i>


00:05:34.583 --> 00:05:38.883
<i>we withdrew from the other worlds</i>
<i>and returned home</i>


00:05:39.021 --> 00:05:41.148
<i>to the Realm Eternal,</i>


00:05:42.524 --> 00:05:44.151
<i>Asgard.</i>


00:06:15.757 --> 00:06:18.419
<i>Here we remain as a beacon of hope,</i>


00:06:19.561 --> 00:06:22.359
<i>shining out across the stars.</i>


00:06:23.432 --> 00:06:26.731
<i>And though we have fallen</i>
<i>into man's myths and legends,</i>


00:06:28.103 --> 00:06:30.298
<i>it was Asgard</i>


00:06:30.439 --> 00:06:32.407
<i>and its warriors</i>


00:06:32.507 --> 00:06:33.940
<i>that brought peace</i>


00:06:34.676 --> 00:06:35.700
to the universe.


00:06:39.781 --> 00:06:42.409
But the day will come


00:06:43.652 --> 00:06:45.279
when one of you


00:06:46.421 --> 00:06:48.218
will have to defend that peace.


00:06:48.991 --> 00:06:51.118
Do the Frost Giants still live?


00:06:51.493 --> 00:06:52.460
When l'm king,


00:06:53.495 --> 00:06:56.464
l'll hunt the monsters down
and slay them all!


00:06:57.599 --> 00:06:59.123
Just as you did, Father.


00:06:59.701 --> 00:07:01.259
A wise king


00:07:01.803 --> 00:07:05.432
never seeks out war.


00:07:10.646 --> 00:07:12.841
But he must always be ready for it.


00:07:24.693 --> 00:07:27.127
-l'm ready, Father.
-So am l.


00:07:28.497 --> 00:07:31.091
Only one of you can ascend
to the throne.


00:07:31.199 --> 00:07:35.158
But both of you were born to be kings.


00:07:55.857 --> 00:07:57.290
Oh, please.


00:08:53.915 --> 00:08:57.373
Thor Odinson,


00:08:59.154 --> 00:09:00.451
my heir,


00:09:03.425 --> 00:09:05.416
my firstborn.


00:09:06.261 --> 00:09:11.699
So long entrusted with
the mighty hammer Mjolnir,


00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:14.860
forged in the heart of a dying star,


00:09:15.470 --> 00:09:18.200
its power has no equal,


00:09:18.306 --> 00:09:20.968
as a weapon to destroy


00:09:21.109 --> 00:09:23.270
or as a tool to build.


00:09:23.945 --> 00:09:26.573
'Tis a fit companion for a king.


00:09:28.116 --> 00:09:30.641
l have defended Asgard


00:09:30.786 --> 00:09:34.813
and the lives of the innocent
across the Nine Realms


00:09:34.956 --> 00:09:37.288
<i>from the time of the great beginning.</i>


00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:39.627
<i>Though the day has come...</i>


00:10:06.121 --> 00:10:08.954
Do you swear to guard
the Nine Realms?


00:10:09.624 --> 00:10:10.591
l swear.


00:10:10.725 --> 00:10:13.853
And do you swear
to preserve the peace?


00:10:14.162 --> 00:10:15.459
l swear.


00:10:15.730 --> 00:10:17.527
Do you swear


00:10:18.567 --> 00:10:21.161
to cast aside all selfish ambition


00:10:21.336 --> 00:10:24.134
and to pledge yourself only
to the good of the Realms?


00:10:24.239 --> 00:10:25.365
l swear!


00:10:25.674 --> 00:10:28.040
Then, on this day,


00:10:28.176 --> 00:10:30.770
l, Odin Allfather,


00:10:32.347 --> 00:10:33.837
proclaim you...


00:10:47.529 --> 00:10:48.655
The Frost Giants!


00:11:34.042 --> 00:11:36.010
The Jotuns must pay
for what they've done!


00:11:36.111 --> 00:11:38.409
They have paid, with their lives.


00:11:39.614 --> 00:11:41.582
The Destroyer did its work,


00:11:41.950 --> 00:11:43.918
the Casket is safe, and all is well.


00:11:44.286 --> 00:11:45.253
All is well?


00:11:46.288 --> 00:11:48.779
They broke into the weapons vault!


00:11:48.924 --> 00:11:51.449
lf the Frost Giants had stolen
even one of these relics...


00:11:51.593 --> 00:11:53.788
-They didn't.
-Well, l want to know why!


00:11:56.498 --> 00:11:58.796
l have a truce with Laufey,
King of the Jotuns.


00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:03.469
He just broke your truce!
They know you are vulnerable!


00:12:04.005 --> 00:12:05.529
What action would you take?


00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:08.973
March into Jotunheim as you once did.
Teach them a lesson.


00:12:09.411 --> 00:12:10.469
Break their spirits


00:12:10.612 --> 00:12:12.705
so they'll never dare
try to cross our borders again.


00:12:12.814 --> 00:12:14.076
You're thinking only as a warrior.


00:12:14.182 --> 00:12:15.410
This was an act of war!


00:12:15.517 --> 00:12:17.747
lt was the act of but a few,
doomed to fail.


00:12:17.852 --> 00:12:19.319
Look how far they got!


00:12:19.454 --> 00:12:21.786
We will find the breach in our defenses
and it will be sealed.


00:12:21.957 --> 00:12:23.254
As King of Asgard...


00:12:23.358 --> 00:12:26.088
But you're not king!


00:12:29.030 --> 00:12:30.327
Not yet.


00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:05.099
lt's unwise to be in my company
right now, Brother.


00:13:06.201 --> 00:13:08.999
This was to be my day of triumph.


00:13:11.239 --> 00:13:12.536
lt'll come.


00:13:13.875 --> 00:13:15.137
ln time.


00:13:15.243 --> 00:13:17.473
What's this?


00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:22.040
lf it's any consolation,
l think you're right.


00:13:22.183 --> 00:13:24.981
About the Frost Giants,
about Laufey, about everything.


00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:28.946
lf they found a way to penetrate
Asgard's defenses once,


00:13:29.057 --> 00:13:30.547
who's to say they won't try again?


00:13:30.692 --> 00:13:32.683
-Next time with an army.
-Exactly.


00:13:32.861 --> 00:13:35.557
There's nothing you can do
without defying Father.


00:13:37.766 --> 00:13:39.563
No, no, no. l know that look.


00:13:39.768 --> 00:13:41.861
That's the only way
to ensure the safety of our borders.


00:13:42.003 --> 00:13:43.027
Thor, it's madness.


00:13:43.571 --> 00:13:45.971
Madness? What sort of madness?


00:13:46.441 --> 00:13:48.238
We're going to Jotunheim.


00:13:49.744 --> 00:13:50.870
What?


00:13:51.446 --> 00:13:53.175
This isn't like a journey to Earth


00:13:53.281 --> 00:13:55.306
where you summon
a little lightning and thunder,


00:13:55.417 --> 00:13:58.045
and the mortals worship you as a god.


00:13:58.186 --> 00:13:59.414
This is Jotunheim.


00:13:59.587 --> 00:14:01.817
My father fought his way into Jotunheim,


00:14:01.923 --> 00:14:04.653
defeated their armies
and took their Casket.


00:14:04.926 --> 00:14:06.393
We would just be looking for answers.


00:14:06.528 --> 00:14:07.756
lt is forbidden!


00:14:10.098 --> 00:14:13.090
My friends, have you forgotten
all that we have done together?


00:14:13.468 --> 00:14:15.231
Fandral, Hogun.


00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:18.203
Who led you
into the most glorious of battles?


00:14:18.873 --> 00:14:20.170
You did.


00:14:20.475 --> 00:14:22.568
And Volstagg,
to delicacies so succulent,


00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:25.235
you thought you'd died
and gone to Valhalla?


00:14:26.714 --> 00:14:27.681
You did.


00:14:27.782 --> 00:14:28.771
Yes!


00:14:28.917 --> 00:14:30.851
And who proved wrong
all who scoffed at the idea


00:14:30.952 --> 00:14:33.386
that a young maiden could be
one of the fiercest warriors


00:14:33.488 --> 00:14:34.455
this realm has ever known?


00:14:34.589 --> 00:14:35.556
l did.


00:14:35.957 --> 00:14:38.585
True, but l supported you, Sif.


00:14:38.726 --> 00:14:40.023
My friends,


00:14:40.462 --> 00:14:42.430
we're going to Jotunheim.


00:15:33.681 --> 00:15:34.841
You leave this to me.


00:15:36.551 --> 00:15:39.145
-Good Heimdall...
-You're not dressed warmly enough.


00:15:39.287 --> 00:15:40.345
l'm sorry?


00:15:40.522 --> 00:15:43.252
Do you think that you can deceive me?


00:15:43.958 --> 00:15:45.255
-You must be mistaken...
-Enough!


00:15:49.397 --> 00:15:50.921
Heimdall, may we pass?


00:15:51.299 --> 00:15:57.499
Never has an enemy slipped my watch
until this day.


00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:01.008
l wish to know how that happened.


00:16:01.142 --> 00:16:03.702
Then tell no one where we have gone
until we've returned.


00:16:03.845 --> 00:16:05.642
Understand?


00:16:10.051 --> 00:16:12.281
What happened?
Silver tongue turn to lead?


00:16:57.065 --> 00:16:58.362
Be warned.


00:16:58.633 --> 00:17:03.036
l will honor my sworn oath
to protect this realm as its Gatekeeper.


00:17:03.471 --> 00:17:06.497
lf your return
threatens the safety of Asgard,


00:17:06.608 --> 00:17:08.940
Bifrost will remain closed to you


00:17:09.244 --> 00:17:12.509
and you'll be left to die
in the cold waste of Jotunheim.


00:17:12.614 --> 00:17:14.548
Couldn't you just
leave the bridge open for us?


00:17:14.649 --> 00:17:15.911
To leave the bridge open


00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:17.285
would unleash
the full power of the Bifrost


00:17:17.285 --> 00:17:18.183
would unleash
the full power of the Bifrost


00:17:18.286 --> 00:17:21.255
and destroy Jotunheim with you upon it.


00:17:21.723 --> 00:17:23.623
l have no plans to die today.


00:17:23.758 --> 00:17:25.419
None do.


00:18:11.506 --> 00:18:12.973
We shouldn't be here.


00:18:15.209 --> 00:18:16.767
Let's move.


00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:16.967
Where are they?


00:19:17.105 --> 00:19:18.367
Hiding,


00:19:18.506 --> 00:19:20.030
as cowards always do.


00:19:30.518 --> 00:19:34.750
You've come a long way to die,
Asgardians.


00:19:34.889 --> 00:19:37.380
l am Thor Odinson!


00:19:37.525 --> 00:19:39.493
We know who you are.


00:19:39.794 --> 00:19:42.160
How did your people get into Asgard?


00:19:51.539 --> 00:19:55.600
The House of Odin is full of traitors.


00:19:55.743 --> 00:19:58.211
Do not dishonor my father's name
with your lies!


00:19:59.080 --> 00:20:02.106
Your father is a murderer and a thief!


00:20:02.383 --> 00:20:05.580
And why have you come here?
To make peace?


00:20:05.887 --> 00:20:08.913
You long for battle. You crave it.


00:20:09.624 --> 00:20:11.524
You're nothing but a boy


00:20:11.793 --> 00:20:14.193
trying to prove himself a man.


00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:18.893
Well, this ''boy''
has grown tired of your mockery.


00:20:25.673 --> 00:20:28.039
Thor, stop and think.


00:20:28.342 --> 00:20:29.809
Look around you, we're outnumbered.


00:20:29.944 --> 00:20:31.605
Know your place, Brother.


00:20:31.746 --> 00:20:35.273
You know not
what your actions would unleash.


00:20:38.019 --> 00:20:39.281
l do.


00:20:40.188 --> 00:20:44.147
Go now, while l still allow it.


00:20:55.036 --> 00:20:58.164
We will accept your most gracious offer.


00:21:10.852 --> 00:21:12.285
Come on, Brother.


00:21:17.825 --> 00:21:20.020
Run back home, little princess.


00:21:20.528 --> 00:21:21.495
Damn.


00:21:27.034 --> 00:21:28.126
Next?


00:21:47.388 --> 00:21:49.515
At least make it a challenge for me!


00:22:09.944 --> 00:22:11.536
That's more like it.


00:22:47.381 --> 00:22:48.439
Don't let them touch you!


00:23:30.658 --> 00:23:32.592
Thor!


00:23:33.995 --> 00:23:35.963
-We must go!
-Then go!


00:23:59.720 --> 00:24:01.187
Run!


00:24:03.190 --> 00:24:04.487
Thor!


00:25:10.257 --> 00:25:11.554
Heimdall!


00:25:11.926 --> 00:25:13.553
Open the bridge!


00:26:19.093 --> 00:26:21.721
Father! We'll finish them together!


00:26:21.929 --> 00:26:23.226
Silence!


00:26:29.036 --> 00:26:30.594
Allfather.


00:26:31.972 --> 00:26:34.099
You look weary.


00:26:36.010 --> 00:26:37.409
Laufey,


00:26:37.545 --> 00:26:39.308
end this now.


00:26:39.446 --> 00:26:41.437
Your boy sought this out.


00:26:42.149 --> 00:26:43.343
You're right.


00:26:45.019 --> 00:26:47.920
And these are the actions of a boy,
treat them as such.


00:26:48.856 --> 00:26:53.156
You and l can end this here and now,
before there's further bloodshed.


00:26:53.294 --> 00:26:56.923
We are beyond diplomacy now,
Allfather.


00:26:58.399 --> 00:27:00.663
He'll get what he came for.


00:27:00.801 --> 00:27:01.790
War


00:27:02.403 --> 00:27:03.870
and death.


00:27:05.472 --> 00:27:06.996
So be it.


00:27:30.598 --> 00:27:31.690
Why did you bring us back?


00:27:31.832 --> 00:27:33.163
Do you realize what you've done?
What you've started?


00:27:33.267 --> 00:27:36.327
-l was protecting my home.
-You cannot even protect your friends!


00:27:36.437 --> 00:27:38.166
How can you hope
to protect a kingdom?


00:27:38.272 --> 00:27:39.967
Get him to the healing room! Now!


00:27:40.074 --> 00:27:43.840
There won't be a kingdom to protect
if you're afraid to act.


00:27:44.612 --> 00:27:48.412
The Jotuns must learn to fear me,
just as they once feared you.


00:27:48.782 --> 00:27:51.148
That's pride and vanity talking,
not leadership.


00:27:51.352 --> 00:27:54.253
You've forgotten everything l taught you
about a warrior's patience.


00:27:54.388 --> 00:27:58.017
While you wait and be patient,
the Nine Realms laugh at us.


00:27:58.359 --> 00:27:59.485
The old ways are done.


00:27:59.593 --> 00:28:02.221
You'd stand giving speeches
while Asgard falls.


00:28:02.363 --> 00:28:05.821
You are a vain, greedy, cruel boy!


00:28:05.966 --> 00:28:08.935
And you are an old man and a fool!


00:28:15.643 --> 00:28:16.940
Yes.


00:28:17.811 --> 00:28:19.438
l was a fool


00:28:20.547 --> 00:28:21.707
to think you were ready.


00:28:22.383 --> 00:28:23.350
Father...


00:28:26.987 --> 00:28:29.956
Thor Odinson,


00:28:31.725 --> 00:28:34.717
you have betrayed
the express command of your king.


00:28:35.095 --> 00:28:37.586
Through your arrogance and stupidity,


00:28:37.731 --> 00:28:40.564
you've opened these peaceful realms
and innocent lives


00:28:40.668 --> 00:28:44.365
to the horror and desolation of war!


00:28:50.444 --> 00:28:54.312
You are unworthy of these realms!


00:28:54.648 --> 00:28:57.242
You're unworthy of your title!


00:28:57.351 --> 00:28:58.978
You're unworthy


00:29:01.622 --> 00:29:06.116
of the loved ones you have betrayed.


00:29:16.470 --> 00:29:18.597
l now take from you your power!


00:29:19.707 --> 00:29:22.767
ln the name of my father


00:29:22.876 --> 00:29:25.071
and his father before,


00:29:25.379 --> 00:29:28.007
l, Odin Allfather, cast you out!


00:29:34.788 --> 00:29:37.951
Whosoever holds this hammer,
if he be worthy,


00:29:38.058 --> 00:29:39.685
shall possess the power of Thor.


00:30:04.852 --> 00:30:06.444
l think that was legally your fault.


00:30:06.553 --> 00:30:08.180
Get the first aid kit.


00:30:08.389 --> 00:30:09.686
Do me a favor and don't be dead.


00:30:15.596 --> 00:30:17.791
Does he need CPR?
Because l totally know CPR.


00:30:30.677 --> 00:30:32.144
Where did he come from?


00:30:36.050 --> 00:30:37.039
You all right?


00:30:37.251 --> 00:30:38.218
Hammer?


00:30:38.552 --> 00:30:39.519
Hammer?


00:30:39.620 --> 00:30:41.713
Yeah, we can tell you're hammered.
lt's pretty obvious.


00:30:42.623 --> 00:30:44.750
Oh, my God. Erik, look at this!


00:30:44.892 --> 00:30:47.656
We have to move quickly
before this all changes.


00:30:48.695 --> 00:30:50.390
Jane, we have to take him
to the hospital.


00:30:50.597 --> 00:30:52.895
-Father!
-He's fine, look at him.


00:30:53.033 --> 00:30:56.992
Heimdall! l know you can hear me!
Open the Bifrost!


00:30:57.104 --> 00:30:59.004
Hospital. You go, l'll stay.


00:30:59.106 --> 00:31:01.574
You. What realm is this?


00:31:01.708 --> 00:31:03.175
Alfheim? Nornheim?


00:31:03.310 --> 00:31:04.277
New Mexico?


00:31:04.545 --> 00:31:08.709
You dare threaten me, Thor,
with so puny a weapon?


00:31:12.252 --> 00:31:14.220
What? He was freaking me out!


00:31:14.455 --> 00:31:16.685
Next time
you decide to taser somebody,


00:31:16.790 --> 00:31:19.190
make sure he's already in the car, okay?


00:31:20.394 --> 00:31:22.453
Jane! Come on.


00:31:40.347 --> 00:31:41.541
Name?


00:31:41.648 --> 00:31:44.139
He said it was Thor?


00:31:44.318 --> 00:31:47.481
T-H-O-R.


00:31:47.988 --> 00:31:50.582
-And your relationship to him?
-l've never met him before.


00:31:50.691 --> 00:31:52.158
Until she hit him with a car.


00:31:52.326 --> 00:31:54.954
l grazed him, but she tasered him.


00:31:55.295 --> 00:31:56.592
Yes, l did.


00:31:58.332 --> 00:31:59.299
Hi.


00:32:00.701 --> 00:32:01.725
Just taking a little blood.


00:32:01.935 --> 00:32:04.165
How dare you attack the son of Odin?


00:32:04.304 --> 00:32:06.135
l need some help!


00:32:07.141 --> 00:32:08.768
Call security!


00:32:09.042 --> 00:32:11.169
Security to ER 3, stat!


00:32:25.058 --> 00:32:27.151
You're no match for the Mighty...


00:33:29.022 --> 00:33:31.490
<i>You don't think</i>
<i>this was just a magnetic storm, do you?</i>


00:33:31.792 --> 00:33:34.556
Look, the lensing around these edges


00:33:34.728 --> 00:33:37.060
is characteristic
of an Einstein-Rosen Bridge.


00:33:37.297 --> 00:33:38.321
A what?


00:33:38.432 --> 00:33:40.491
-l thought you were a science major?
-Political science.


00:33:40.601 --> 00:33:42.398
She was the only applicant.


00:33:42.536 --> 00:33:45.164
An Einstein-Rosen Bridge
is a theoretical connection


00:33:45.272 --> 00:33:46.500
between two different points
of space-time.


00:33:46.607 --> 00:33:47.904
lt's a wormhole.


00:33:48.041 --> 00:33:51.010
-Erik, look. What do you see?
-Stars.


00:33:51.111 --> 00:33:52.908
Yeah, but not our stars.


00:33:53.046 --> 00:33:56.743
See, this is the star alignment
for our quadrant this time of year,


00:33:56.883 --> 00:33:59.943
and unless Ursa Minor decided
to take a day off,


00:34:00.087 --> 00:34:02.248
these are
someone else's constellations.


00:34:02.389 --> 00:34:04.186
Hey! Check this out.


00:34:10.998 --> 00:34:12.761
No, it can't be.


00:34:14.768 --> 00:34:16.929
l think l left something at the hospital.


00:34:32.419 --> 00:34:34.546
lt's not possible!


00:34:48.468 --> 00:34:50.936
He was on drugs or something.
He just went nuts.


00:34:59.613 --> 00:35:01.240
Oh, my God.


00:35:04.618 --> 00:35:06.779
l just lost
my most important piece of evidence.


00:35:06.887 --> 00:35:07.911
Typical.


00:35:08.021 --> 00:35:10.148
-So now what?
-We find him.


00:35:10.290 --> 00:35:11.621
Did you see what he did in there?


00:35:11.725 --> 00:35:13.488
l'm not sure finding him is the best idea.


00:35:13.627 --> 00:35:15.925
Well, our data can't tell us
what it was like to be inside that event,


00:35:16.029 --> 00:35:18.657
and he can. So, we're gonna find him.


00:35:18.799 --> 00:35:19.788
Okay.


00:35:19.900 --> 00:35:22.494
So we're gonna look
all over New Mexico, right?


00:35:22.636 --> 00:35:23.933
Exactly.


00:35:28.241 --> 00:35:29.208
What?


00:35:30.310 --> 00:35:33.438
l'm so sorry.
l swear l'm not doing this on purpose.


00:35:50.564 --> 00:35:52.122
l got it, l got it.


00:36:01.942 --> 00:36:03.739
Come on, kick it in now!


00:36:12.452 --> 00:36:13.646
Did it work?


00:36:35.475 --> 00:36:37.568
Sir, we found it.


00:36:43.884 --> 00:36:48.184
You know, for a crazy homeless person,
he's pretty cut.


00:36:51.324 --> 00:36:53.292
Hey, sorry l tased you!


00:36:55.762 --> 00:36:57.730
Excuse me, excuse me!


00:37:05.105 --> 00:37:06.470
What is this?


00:37:09.443 --> 00:37:10.637
My ex.


00:37:11.244 --> 00:37:15.203
Good with patients
and bad with relationships.


00:37:16.249 --> 00:37:17.716
They're the only clothes l had
that would fit you.


00:37:17.818 --> 00:37:18.807
They will suffice.


00:37:19.953 --> 00:37:20.920
You're welcome.


00:37:21.021 --> 00:37:22.454
This mortal form has grown weak.


00:37:23.356 --> 00:37:24.380
l need sustenance.


00:37:43.877 --> 00:37:45.435
We should never have let him go.


00:37:45.712 --> 00:37:47.179
There was no stopping him.


00:37:47.314 --> 00:37:49.248
Well, at least he's only banished,
not dead.


00:37:49.349 --> 00:37:50.611
Which is what we'd all be


00:37:50.717 --> 00:37:53.413
if that guard hadn't told Odin
where we'd gone.


00:37:59.826 --> 00:38:01.293
How did the guard even know?


00:38:01.828 --> 00:38:02.852
l told him.


00:38:04.364 --> 00:38:05.353
What?


00:38:05.499 --> 00:38:08.024
l told him to go to Odin after we'd left.


00:38:08.235 --> 00:38:09.532
He should be flogged for taking so long.


00:38:09.669 --> 00:38:11.159
We should never have
reached Jotunheim.


00:38:11.304 --> 00:38:12.293
You told the guard?


00:38:12.506 --> 00:38:14.371
l saved our lives.


00:38:14.508 --> 00:38:16.305
And Thor's.


00:38:16.409 --> 00:38:18.843
l had no idea Father would banish him
for what he did.


00:38:20.080 --> 00:38:21.047
Loki.


00:38:21.915 --> 00:38:24.611
You must go to the Allfather
and convince him to change his mind.


00:38:24.784 --> 00:38:27.309
And if l do, then what?


00:38:27.420 --> 00:38:30.218
l love Thor more dearly than any of you,
but you know what he is.


00:38:30.857 --> 00:38:33.451
He's arrogant.
He's reckless. He's dangerous.


00:38:33.560 --> 00:38:35.494
You saw how he was today.


00:38:35.829 --> 00:38:37.228
ls that what Asgard needs from its king?


00:38:41.868 --> 00:38:46.737
He may speak of the good of Asgard,
but he's always been jealous of Thor.


00:38:47.774 --> 00:38:49.901
We should be grateful to him,
he saved our lives.


00:38:50.210 --> 00:38:52.075
Laufey said


00:38:52.212 --> 00:38:54.680
there were traitors in the House of Odin.


00:38:55.448 --> 00:38:59.578
A master of magic
could bring three Jotuns into Asgard.


00:39:01.454 --> 00:39:03.081
Loki's always been one for mischief,


00:39:03.223 --> 00:39:05.589
but you're talking
about something else entirely.


00:39:26.146 --> 00:39:27.443
Stop!


00:39:31.151 --> 00:39:32.618
Am l cursed?


00:39:32.986 --> 00:39:34.112
No.


00:39:38.325 --> 00:39:39.451
What am l?


00:39:40.660 --> 00:39:41.957
You're my son.


00:39:52.172 --> 00:39:54.140
What more than that?


00:39:58.945 --> 00:40:01.573
The Casket wasn't the only thing
you took from Jotunheim that day,


00:40:01.681 --> 00:40:02.648
was it?


00:40:09.456 --> 00:40:10.753
No.


00:40:12.626 --> 00:40:13.923
ln the aftermath of the battle,


00:40:14.027 --> 00:40:16.825
l went into the temple
and l found a baby.


00:40:21.368 --> 00:40:24.166
<i>Small for a giant's offspring.</i>


00:40:24.804 --> 00:40:27.500
<i>Abandoned, suffering, left to die.</i>


00:40:28.708 --> 00:40:30.175
<i>Laufey's son.</i>


00:40:32.045 --> 00:40:33.672
Laufey's son.


00:40:37.217 --> 00:40:38.514
Yes.


00:40:42.055 --> 00:40:43.113
Why?


00:40:43.556 --> 00:40:46.855
You were knee-deep in Jotun blood,
why would you take me?


00:40:46.993 --> 00:40:48.460
You were an innocent child.


00:40:48.561 --> 00:40:52.520
No. You took me for a purpose.
What was it?


00:40:56.236 --> 00:40:58.204
Tell me!


00:40:59.906 --> 00:41:02.704
l thought
we could unite our kingdoms one day.


00:41:03.076 --> 00:41:06.136
Bring about an alliance,
bring about permanent peace.


00:41:06.513 --> 00:41:07.810
Through you.


00:41:07.914 --> 00:41:09.040
What?


00:41:10.083 --> 00:41:12.483
But those plans no longer matter.


00:41:14.087 --> 00:41:17.318
So l am no more
than another stolen relic,


00:41:17.424 --> 00:41:19.858
locked up here
until you might have use of me.


00:41:19.993 --> 00:41:21.392
Why do you twist my words?


00:41:21.528 --> 00:41:23.496
You could have told me what l was
from the beginning,


00:41:23.596 --> 00:41:24.563
why didn't you?


00:41:24.864 --> 00:41:25.990
You're my son.


00:41:26.599 --> 00:41:28.658
l wanted only to protect you
from the truth.


00:41:30.036 --> 00:41:31.731
Because l'm the monster


00:41:31.871 --> 00:41:33.896
parents tell their children about
at night?


00:41:34.207 --> 00:41:36.072
-No, no.
-You know, it all makes sense now!


00:41:36.209 --> 00:41:38.905
Why you favored Thor all these years!


00:41:39.045 --> 00:41:41.878
Because no matter how much
you claim to love me,


00:41:42.382 --> 00:41:45.579
you could never have a Frost Giant
sitting on the throne of Asgard!


00:42:05.638 --> 00:42:06.935
Guards!


00:42:07.807 --> 00:42:09.934
Guards, please, help!


00:42:15.815 --> 00:42:17.544
How'd you get inside that cloud?


00:42:17.817 --> 00:42:20.285
Also, how could you eat
an entire box of Pop-Tarts


00:42:20.420 --> 00:42:21.910
and still be this hungry?


00:42:27.761 --> 00:42:30.093
-This drink, l like it.
-l know. lt's great, right?


00:42:30.230 --> 00:42:31.288
Another!


00:42:32.665 --> 00:42:34.394
Sorry, lzzy. Little accident.


00:42:38.004 --> 00:42:40.063
-What was that?
-lt was delicious. l want another.


00:42:40.173 --> 00:42:42.368
-Well, you could have just said so.
-l just did.


00:42:42.509 --> 00:42:45.876
-No, l mean, ask nicely.
-l meant no disrespect.


00:42:45.979 --> 00:42:47.037
All right. Well, no more smashing.


00:42:47.580 --> 00:42:48.604
Deal?


00:42:51.117 --> 00:42:52.084
You have my word.


00:42:53.353 --> 00:42:54.377
Good.


00:42:55.789 --> 00:42:57.620
The usual, please, lzzy.


00:42:57.791 --> 00:43:00.259
You missed all the excitement
out at the crater.


00:43:00.693 --> 00:43:03.753
They're saying some kind of satellite
landed out in the desert.


00:43:03.863 --> 00:43:05.728
Yeah, we were having
a good time with it


00:43:06.166 --> 00:43:07.497
until the Feds showed up.


00:43:07.634 --> 00:43:10.432
Excuse me.
Did you say there was a satellite crash?


00:43:10.537 --> 00:43:11.561
Yeah.


00:43:11.671 --> 00:43:14.071
Oh, my God. This is going on Facebook.
Smile.


00:43:16.476 --> 00:43:18.341
What did it look like, the satellite?


00:43:19.212 --> 00:43:22.113
l don't know anything about satellites,
but it was heavy.


00:43:22.882 --> 00:43:26.340
l mean, nobody could lift it.


00:43:26.486 --> 00:43:29.114
They said it was radioactive.
l had my hands all over it.


00:43:29.389 --> 00:43:30.856
Which way?


00:43:33.059 --> 00:43:35.027
Fifty miles west of here.


00:43:35.395 --> 00:43:37.090
Well, l wouldn't waste my time!


00:43:37.197 --> 00:43:38.926
Looked like the whole Army
was coming when we left.


00:43:44.037 --> 00:43:45.334
Dumbass!


00:43:46.206 --> 00:43:47.503
Where are you going?


00:43:47.907 --> 00:43:49.932
-Fifty miles west of here.
-Why?


00:43:50.043 --> 00:43:53.376
-To get what belongs to me.
-So you own a satellite now?


00:43:53.513 --> 00:43:54.480
lt's not what they say it is.


00:43:54.581 --> 00:43:55.605
Well, whatever it is,


00:43:55.715 --> 00:43:57.012
the government seems to think
it's theirs.


00:43:57.150 --> 00:43:59.141
So, you just intend to go in there
and take it?


00:43:59.252 --> 00:44:00.310
Yes.


00:44:01.821 --> 00:44:02.981
lf you take me there now,


00:44:03.089 --> 00:44:04.716
l'll tell you everything you wish to know.


00:44:05.158 --> 00:44:06.318
-Everything?
-Yes.


00:44:06.426 --> 00:44:09.190
All the answers you seek will be yours
once l reclaim Mjolnir.


00:44:09.329 --> 00:44:11.320
Myeu-muh? What's Myeu-muh?


00:44:11.431 --> 00:44:13.365
Can l have a word, Jane?


00:44:17.437 --> 00:44:18.904
Please don't do this.


00:44:19.372 --> 00:44:21.067
You saw what l saw last night.


00:44:21.207 --> 00:44:23.573
This is no coincidence.
We have to find out what's in that crater.


00:44:23.710 --> 00:44:25.644
But l'm not talking about the crater,
l'm talking about him.


00:44:25.745 --> 00:44:28.407
-But he's promising us the answers.
-He's delusional.


00:44:28.548 --> 00:44:29.537
Listen to what he's saying.


00:44:29.682 --> 00:44:33.550
He's talking about Mjolnir
and Thor and Bifrost.


00:44:33.920 --> 00:44:36.081
lt's the stories l grew up with as a child.


00:44:36.222 --> 00:44:39.020
l'm just going to drive him. That's it.


00:44:39.259 --> 00:44:41.227
He's dangerous, Jane.


00:44:47.200 --> 00:44:50.067
l'm sorry, but l can't take you.


00:44:50.203 --> 00:44:51.602
Then this is where we say goodbye.


00:45:02.115 --> 00:45:03.742
Thank you?


00:45:04.550 --> 00:45:06.245
Jane Foster,


00:45:06.386 --> 00:45:07.910
Erik Selvig,


00:45:08.054 --> 00:45:09.521
Darcy,


00:45:09.756 --> 00:45:11.053
farewell.


00:45:14.727 --> 00:45:16.024
All right.


00:45:16.729 --> 00:45:18.253
Back to work.


00:45:38.751 --> 00:45:40.275
That's my stuff!


00:45:45.024 --> 00:45:46.286
What the hell is going on here?


00:45:46.426 --> 00:45:48.394
Ms. Foster,
l'm Agent Coulson with S.H.l.E.L.D.


00:45:48.494 --> 00:45:50.121
ls that supposed to mean something
to me?


00:45:50.263 --> 00:45:51.491
-You can't do this!
-Jane!


00:45:51.931 --> 00:45:54.729
Jane, this is a lot more serious
than you realize. Let it go.


00:45:54.834 --> 00:45:56.825
Let it go? This is my life.


00:45:57.136 --> 00:45:59.161
We're investigating a security threat.


00:45:59.305 --> 00:46:01.967
We need to appropriate your records
and all your atmospheric data.


00:46:02.108 --> 00:46:04.474
By ''appropriate,'' do you mean steal?


00:46:04.610 --> 00:46:06.271
Here, this should
more than compensate you


00:46:06.379 --> 00:46:07.346
for your trouble.


00:46:07.513 --> 00:46:10.004
l can't just buy replacements
at Radio Shack,


00:46:10.149 --> 00:46:11.810
l made most of this equipment myself!


00:46:11.951 --> 00:46:13.248
Then l'm sure you can do it again.


00:46:13.353 --> 00:46:16.447
And l'm sure l can sue you
for violating my constitutional rights!


00:46:16.556 --> 00:46:19.024
l'm sorry, Ms. Foster,
but we're the good guys.


00:46:19.158 --> 00:46:21.183
So are we!


00:46:21.327 --> 00:46:24.490
l'm on the verge of understanding
something extraordinary.


00:46:24.630 --> 00:46:26.359
And everything l know
about this phenomenon


00:46:26.499 --> 00:46:28.330
is either in this lab or in this book.


00:46:28.468 --> 00:46:31.130
And you can't just take this away... Hey!


00:46:32.071 --> 00:46:35.006
Jane! Easy! Easy. Jane...


00:46:37.477 --> 00:46:39.274
Thank you for your cooperation.


00:46:57.163 --> 00:46:58.960
Years of research,


00:46:59.065 --> 00:47:00.032
gone.


00:47:00.500 --> 00:47:02.968
They even took my iPod.


00:47:03.069 --> 00:47:05.697
-What about the backups?
-They took our backups.


00:47:06.005 --> 00:47:09.463
They took the backups of our backups.
They were extremely thorough.


00:47:09.575 --> 00:47:11.873
l just downloaded, like,
30 songs onto there.


00:47:12.011 --> 00:47:14.878
Could you please stop with your iPod?


00:47:15.448 --> 00:47:17.575
Who are these people?


00:47:19.218 --> 00:47:21.049
l knew this scientist.


00:47:21.621 --> 00:47:24.089
The pioneer in gamma radiation.


00:47:24.223 --> 00:47:26.316
S.H.l.E.L.D. showed up


00:47:27.593 --> 00:47:29.220
and he wasn't heard from again.


00:47:30.096 --> 00:47:33.497
They're not gonna do that to us.
l'm gonna get everything back.


00:47:33.599 --> 00:47:36.363
Come on, please.
Let me contact one of my colleagues.


00:47:36.536 --> 00:47:38.936
He's had some dealings
with these people before.


00:47:39.238 --> 00:47:41.672
l'll e-mail him and maybe he can help.


00:47:42.742 --> 00:47:44.175
They took your laptop, too.


00:47:52.885 --> 00:47:55.854
Allfather,
we must speak with you urgently.


00:48:08.734 --> 00:48:10.702
My friends.


00:48:11.070 --> 00:48:12.697
Where's Odin?


00:48:12.972 --> 00:48:15.873
Father has fallen into the Odinsleep.


00:48:17.410 --> 00:48:20.038
Mother fears
he may never awaken again.


00:48:20.580 --> 00:48:21.740
We would speak with her.


00:48:21.981 --> 00:48:25.109
She has refused to leave
my father's bedside.


00:48:27.420 --> 00:48:30.116
You can bring your urgent matter to me.


00:48:37.597 --> 00:48:38.894
Your king.


00:48:50.143 --> 00:48:54.443
My King, we would ask
that you end Thor's banishment.


00:48:59.152 --> 00:49:02.519
My first command
cannot be to undo the Allfather's last.


00:49:05.324 --> 00:49:07.792
We're on the brink of war
with Jotunheim.


00:49:08.995 --> 00:49:11.828
Our people need a sense of continuity,


00:49:11.964 --> 00:49:14.694
in order to feel safe
in these difficult times.


00:49:15.968 --> 00:49:17.697
All of us must stand together


00:49:18.571 --> 00:49:20.198
for the good of Asgard.


00:49:22.708 --> 00:49:24.266
Yes, of course.


00:49:24.644 --> 00:49:27.545
-Good. Then you will wait for my word.
-lf l may


00:49:29.248 --> 00:49:33.708
beg the indulgence of Your Majesty
to perhaps reconsider...


00:49:33.920 --> 00:49:35.046
We're done!


00:50:39.085 --> 00:50:40.052
l need a horse!


00:50:42.321 --> 00:50:45.449
We don't have horses.
Just dogs, cats, birds...


00:50:45.625 --> 00:50:47.786
Then give me one of those
large enough to ride.


00:50:48.461 --> 00:50:49.951
Hey, you still need a lift?


00:50:55.268 --> 00:50:57.896
l've never done anything like this before.


00:50:59.305 --> 00:51:02.638
Have you ever done
anything like this before?


00:51:02.775 --> 00:51:04.242
Many times.


00:51:05.111 --> 00:51:06.578
But you're brave to do it.


00:51:06.679 --> 00:51:09.204
Well, they just stole
my entire life's work.


00:51:09.315 --> 00:51:11.215
l don't really have much left to lose.


00:51:12.618 --> 00:51:13.585
Yeah, but you're clever.


00:51:14.687 --> 00:51:17.588
Far more clever than anyone else
in this realm.


00:51:17.857 --> 00:51:20.223
''Realm''? ''Realm''?


00:51:20.660 --> 00:51:23.390
-You think me strange.
-Yeah, l do.


00:51:23.963 --> 00:51:26.261
Good strange or bad strange?


00:51:26.499 --> 00:51:28.433
l'm not quite sure yet.


00:51:33.472 --> 00:51:35.099
l'm sorry.


00:51:40.279 --> 00:51:41.337
But who are you?


00:51:43.649 --> 00:51:44.946
Really?


00:51:47.520 --> 00:51:48.919
You'll see soon enough.


00:51:49.889 --> 00:51:51.356
You promised me answers.


00:51:55.061 --> 00:51:56.926
What you seek, it's a bridge.


00:51:57.229 --> 00:51:59.163
Like an Einstein-Rosen Bridge?


00:51:59.298 --> 00:52:00.424
More like a Rainbow Bridge.


00:52:03.669 --> 00:52:05.864
God, l hope you're not crazy.


00:52:15.681 --> 00:52:19.048
l never get used to seeing him like this.


00:52:19.185 --> 00:52:22.985
He's put it off for so long now,
that l fear...


00:52:25.524 --> 00:52:27.219
How long will it last?


00:52:27.693 --> 00:52:31.891
l don't know. This time it's different.
We were unprepared.


00:52:34.200 --> 00:52:35.827
So why did he lie?


00:52:36.702 --> 00:52:40.900
He kept the truth from you
so that you would never feel different.


00:52:41.040 --> 00:52:43.338
You are our son, Loki,


00:52:43.876 --> 00:52:45.969
and we, your family.


00:52:47.880 --> 00:52:51.839
We mustn't lose hope
that your father will return to us.


00:52:53.052 --> 00:52:54.519
And your brother.


00:52:55.955 --> 00:52:57.752
What hope is there for Thor?


00:52:58.057 --> 00:53:01.584
There's always a purpose
to everything your father does.


00:53:34.393 --> 00:53:35.951
That's no satellite crash!


00:53:36.095 --> 00:53:37.289
They would have hauled
the wreckage away,


00:53:37.430 --> 00:53:38.954
they wouldn't have built a city around it.


00:53:40.433 --> 00:53:43.891
-You're going to need this.
-What? Wait, why?


00:53:47.273 --> 00:53:48.570
Now stay here.


00:53:49.008 --> 00:53:52.466
Once l have Mjolnir, l will return
the items they've stolen from you.


00:53:52.845 --> 00:53:53.812
Deal?


00:53:54.246 --> 00:53:56.476
No. Look what's down there.


00:53:56.615 --> 00:53:59.448
You think you're just gonna walk in,
grab our stuff and walk out?


00:53:59.585 --> 00:54:01.576
No. l'm going to fly out.


00:54:09.528 --> 00:54:12.258
Sir, feed from the keyhole
can barely penetrate the cloud cover.


00:54:12.631 --> 00:54:13.893
Tech's barely working as it is,


00:54:13.999 --> 00:54:16.160
with all the interference
that thing's giving off.


00:54:16.635 --> 00:54:19.001
And we've got a commercial aircraft
coming right over us.


00:54:19.138 --> 00:54:22.164
Southwest Airlines, flight 5434.


00:54:22.308 --> 00:54:23.297
Reroute it like all the others.


00:54:24.276 --> 00:54:25.265
Hold a sec.


00:54:25.878 --> 00:54:28.676
We've got something outside the fence,
west side.


00:54:28.881 --> 00:54:32.248
<i>Delancey, Jackson.</i>
<i>West side perimeter. Go check it out.</i>


00:54:34.787 --> 00:54:36.084
There it is.


00:54:44.897 --> 00:54:46.489
Delancey, Jackson. Report.


00:54:54.840 --> 00:54:56.705
Agent down.
We've got a perimeter breach.


00:55:09.722 --> 00:55:13.818
<i>You've reached Dr. Erik Selvig.</i>
<i>Please leave me a message.</i>


00:55:14.693 --> 00:55:17.821
Hi, Erik, it's me. Don't worry, l'm fine,


00:55:18.197 --> 00:55:20.529
but just in case
you don't hear from me in the next hour,


00:55:20.666 --> 00:55:23.499
just come by the crater site
and try and find me, okay?


00:55:23.602 --> 00:55:26.400
l did exactly what you told me not to.
l'm sorry.


00:55:26.705 --> 00:55:28.172
So sorry. Bye.


00:55:32.044 --> 00:55:33.306
Bravo quadrant, move!


00:55:46.859 --> 00:55:47.917
Entering south tunnel!


00:55:50.095 --> 00:55:51.585
Negative, negative.
l have no comms.


00:56:05.711 --> 00:56:07.508
Target sighted, east tunnel!


00:56:07.780 --> 00:56:09.441
l need eyes up high, with a gun.


00:56:35.274 --> 00:56:36.434
Moving north!


00:56:44.450 --> 00:56:45.417
What have we got?


00:56:45.517 --> 00:56:46.984
There's a massive
electromagnetic surge


00:56:47.119 --> 00:56:48.211
coming off that thing.


00:56:48.320 --> 00:56:50.083
Systems are barely coping.


00:56:50.289 --> 00:56:51.984
Barton? Talk to me.


00:56:53.425 --> 00:56:54.983
You want me to slow him down, sir?


00:56:56.261 --> 00:56:58.456
Or are you sending in more guys
for him to beat up?


00:56:58.697 --> 00:57:00.164
l'll let you know.


00:57:15.047 --> 00:57:16.344
You're big.


00:57:17.483 --> 00:57:18.814
Fought bigger.


00:58:03.362 --> 00:58:07.162
Better call it, Coulson,
'cause l'm starting to root for this guy.


00:58:27.886 --> 00:58:28.853
Last chance, sir.


00:58:28.954 --> 00:58:31.013
<i>Wait. l want to see this.</i>


00:59:40.092 --> 00:59:43.061
All right, show's over.
Ground units, move in.


01:00:35.747 --> 01:00:37.715
He committed a crime. He's in jail!


01:00:37.850 --> 01:00:39.977
-l can't just leave him there!
-Why?


01:00:40.252 --> 01:00:42.220
You didn't see what l saw!


01:00:42.588 --> 01:00:44.556
Look! Look, it's Myeu-muh.


01:00:49.894 --> 01:00:50.519
Where'd you find this?


01:00:50.862 --> 01:00:51.954
The children's section.


01:00:52.063 --> 01:00:54.463
l just wanted to show you
how silly his story was.


01:00:54.565 --> 01:00:56.465
But you're the one
who's always pushing me


01:00:56.567 --> 01:00:58.660
to chase down every possibility,
every alternative!


01:00:58.803 --> 01:01:00.998
l'm talking about science, not magic!


01:01:01.339 --> 01:01:03.330
Well, magic's just science
that we don't understand yet.


01:01:03.474 --> 01:01:06.034
-Arthur C. Clarke.
-Who wrote science fiction.


01:01:06.177 --> 01:01:08.645
-A precursor to science fact!
-ln some cases, yeah.


01:01:08.746 --> 01:01:10.373
Well, if there is
an Einstein-Rosen Bridge,


01:01:10.514 --> 01:01:11.845
then there's something
on the other side.


01:01:11.983 --> 01:01:13.644
And advanced beings
could have crossed it!


01:01:13.851 --> 01:01:14.818
Jane.


01:01:15.019 --> 01:01:17.886
A primitive culture like the Vikings
might have worshipped them as deities.


01:01:18.022 --> 01:01:19.717
Yes! Yes, exactly. Thank you.


01:01:27.531 --> 01:01:28.657
You made my men,


01:01:28.766 --> 01:01:31.200
some of the most
highly trained professionals in the world,


01:01:31.335 --> 01:01:34.065
look like a bunch of minimum-wage
mall cops.


01:01:35.940 --> 01:01:37.134
That's hurtful.


01:01:38.242 --> 01:01:41.678
ln my experience, it takes someone
who's received similar training


01:01:42.179 --> 01:01:43.168
to do what you did to them.


01:01:47.752 --> 01:01:51.313
Pakistan? Chechnya? Afghanistan?


01:01:52.590 --> 01:01:55.821
No, you strike me
more as the soldier of fortune type.


01:01:56.694 --> 01:01:59.492
Where was it? South Africa?


01:02:01.032 --> 01:02:04.900
Certain groups pay very well
for a good mercenary like you.


01:02:07.271 --> 01:02:08.670
Who are you?


01:02:13.611 --> 01:02:16.045
One way or another,
we find out what we need to know.


01:02:16.447 --> 01:02:17.709
We're good at that.


01:02:23.487 --> 01:02:24.784
Don't go anywhere.


01:02:31.295 --> 01:02:33.763
Loki! What are you doing here?


01:02:34.131 --> 01:02:35.598
l had to see you.


01:02:37.301 --> 01:02:38.598
What's happened?


01:02:38.970 --> 01:02:40.938
Tell me. ls it Jotunheim?


01:02:41.305 --> 01:02:42.704
Let me explain to Father.


01:02:42.807 --> 01:02:44.104
Father is dead.


01:02:50.314 --> 01:02:51.611
What?


01:02:53.484 --> 01:02:55.111
Your banishment,


01:02:56.153 --> 01:02:58.280
the threat of a new war,


01:02:59.423 --> 01:03:01.118
it was too much for him to bear.


01:03:03.828 --> 01:03:05.955
You mustn't blame yourself.


01:03:06.831 --> 01:03:08.298
l know that you loved him.


01:03:09.266 --> 01:03:11.962
l tried to tell him so,
but he wouldn't listen.


01:03:14.205 --> 01:03:16.469
lt was so cruel
to put the hammer within your reach,


01:03:16.607 --> 01:03:18.507
knowing that you could never lift it.


01:03:21.879 --> 01:03:24.109
The burden of the throne
has fallen to me now.


01:03:30.721 --> 01:03:32.348
Can l come home?


01:03:33.324 --> 01:03:36.293
The truce with Jotunheim
is conditional upon your exile.


01:03:36.660 --> 01:03:42.758
-Yes, but couldn't we find a way...
-And Mother has forbidden your return.


01:03:46.137 --> 01:03:47.695
This is goodbye, Brother.


01:03:50.174 --> 01:03:52.039
l'm so sorry.


01:03:57.681 --> 01:03:58.807
No.


01:04:00.351 --> 01:04:01.978
l am sorry.


01:04:07.425 --> 01:04:09.655
Thank you for coming here.


01:04:14.198 --> 01:04:15.495
Farewell.


01:04:28.612 --> 01:04:29.840
Goodbye.


01:04:30.881 --> 01:04:31.848
Goodbye?


01:04:32.450 --> 01:04:33.747
l just got back.


01:05:09.753 --> 01:05:10.720
Sir?


01:05:11.655 --> 01:05:12.952
He's got a visitor.


01:05:18.496 --> 01:05:20.123
His name is Donald Blake?


01:05:20.431 --> 01:05:22.058
Dr. Donald Blake.


01:05:22.299 --> 01:05:24.028
You have dangerous coworkers,
Dr. Selvig.


01:05:24.335 --> 01:05:28.135
He was distraught when he found out
that you've taken all our research.


01:05:28.772 --> 01:05:31.240
That was years of his life, gone!


01:05:33.177 --> 01:05:35.475
You can understand
how a man could go off like that.


01:05:35.946 --> 01:05:38.039
A big, faceless organization like yours


01:05:38.149 --> 01:05:40.049
coming in with their
jackbooted thugs and...


01:05:42.286 --> 01:05:43.651
That's how he put it.


01:05:43.854 --> 01:05:44.878
That still doesn't explain


01:05:44.989 --> 01:05:46.581
how he managed
to tear through our security.


01:05:46.957 --> 01:05:50.256
Steroids! He's a bit of a fitness nut.


01:05:51.962 --> 01:05:53.088
Sir?


01:05:57.801 --> 01:05:59.098
lt says here that he's an M.D.


01:05:59.370 --> 01:06:01.634
Well, he is! Or he was.


01:06:01.772 --> 01:06:04.263
He switched careers
and became a physicist.


01:06:04.508 --> 01:06:06.271
A brilliant physicist.


01:06:06.377 --> 01:06:08.572
He's a wonderful man.
He's a man in pain.


01:06:11.148 --> 01:06:13.844
Donny, Donny, Donny!


01:06:14.385 --> 01:06:18.344
There you are. You're gonna be all right.
l'm taking you home now.


01:06:32.836 --> 01:06:34.303
Dr. Selvig!


01:06:35.406 --> 01:06:37.806
Just keep him away from the bars.


01:06:38.342 --> 01:06:39.639
l will!


01:06:41.512 --> 01:06:44.310
-Where are we going?
-To get a drink.


01:06:44.682 --> 01:06:45.979
Follow them.


01:06:52.423 --> 01:06:54.550
You know, l had it all backwards.


01:06:56.694 --> 01:06:58.161
l had it all wrong.


01:07:01.599 --> 01:07:05.228
lt's not a bad thing finding out
that you don't have all the answers.


01:07:05.703 --> 01:07:07.500
You start asking the right questions.


01:07:11.709 --> 01:07:15.668
For the first time in my life,


01:07:15.779 --> 01:07:20.375
l have no idea what l'm supposed to do.


01:07:21.452 --> 01:07:24.387
Anyone who's ever going to
find his way in this world


01:07:24.521 --> 01:07:27.581
has to start by admitting
he doesn't know where the hell he is.


01:07:29.560 --> 01:07:31.084
Thank you for what you've done.


01:07:31.295 --> 01:07:33.593
No, don't thank me. l only did it for Jane.


01:07:35.232 --> 01:07:37.860
Her father and l
taught at university together.


01:07:38.235 --> 01:07:39.759
He was a good man.


01:07:40.804 --> 01:07:41.862
He never listened.


01:07:43.240 --> 01:07:44.764
Neither did l.


01:07:46.076 --> 01:07:48.101
My father
was trying to teach me something,


01:07:48.245 --> 01:07:50.110
but l was too stupid to see it.


01:07:51.248 --> 01:07:55.241
l don't know if you're delusional
or if you're pulling some kind of con,


01:07:55.386 --> 01:07:56.683
l don't care.


01:07:56.787 --> 01:07:58.084
l just care about her.


01:07:59.490 --> 01:08:01.890
l've seen the way she looks at you.


01:08:05.262 --> 01:08:07.787
l swear to you, l mean her no harm.


01:08:08.098 --> 01:08:09.065
Good.


01:08:09.767 --> 01:08:13.726
ln that case, l'll buy you another round,
and you leave town tonight.


01:08:18.942 --> 01:08:20.739
Two boilermakers.


01:09:12.363 --> 01:09:13.921
Kill him.


01:09:15.466 --> 01:09:17.491
After all l've done for you?


01:09:19.903 --> 01:09:24.499
So you're the one
who showed us the way into Asgard.


01:09:24.875 --> 01:09:27.002
That was just a bit of fun, really.


01:09:28.212 --> 01:09:31.181
To ruin my brother's big day.


01:09:32.049 --> 01:09:35.849
And to protect the realm
from his idiotic rule for a while longer.


01:09:37.187 --> 01:09:39.485
l will hear you.


01:09:42.926 --> 01:09:47.363
l will conceal you
and a handful of your soldiers,


01:09:48.065 --> 01:09:53.025
lead you into Odin's chambers,
and you can slay him where he lies.


01:09:53.504 --> 01:09:55.165
Why not kill him yourself?


01:09:57.274 --> 01:09:59.902
l suspect that the Asgardians
would not take kindly


01:10:00.043 --> 01:10:02.238
to a king who had murdered
his predecessor.


01:10:03.447 --> 01:10:06.507
Once Odin is dead,
l will return the Casket to you


01:10:08.619 --> 01:10:11.588
and you can return Jotunheim to all its...


01:10:14.525 --> 01:10:15.822
Glory.


01:10:17.127 --> 01:10:18.424
l...


01:10:19.963 --> 01:10:21.760
Accept.


01:10:27.638 --> 01:10:29.196
What troubles you, Gatekeeper?


01:10:29.473 --> 01:10:34.433
l turned my gaze upon you in Jotunheim,
but could neither see you nor hear you.


01:10:35.145 --> 01:10:36.373
You were shrouded from me,


01:10:36.480 --> 01:10:38.607
like the Frost Giants
that entered this realm.


01:10:38.982 --> 01:10:42.281
Perhaps your senses have weakened
after your many years of service.


01:10:42.419 --> 01:10:44.046
Or perhaps someone has found a way


01:10:44.154 --> 01:10:47.214
to hide that
which he does not wish me to see.


01:10:48.492 --> 01:10:50.551
You have great power, Heimdall.


01:10:53.096 --> 01:10:54.563
Did Odin ever fear you?


01:10:56.834 --> 01:10:58.461
-No.
-And why is that?


01:10:58.769 --> 01:11:01.795
Because he is my king
and l am sworn to obey him.


01:11:02.172 --> 01:11:06.302
He was your king
and you're sworn to obey me now.


01:11:07.177 --> 01:11:08.235
Yes?


01:11:13.784 --> 01:11:15.081
Yes.


01:11:15.819 --> 01:11:18.481
Then you will open the Bifrost to no one


01:11:18.622 --> 01:11:21.420
until l have repaired the damage
that my brother has done.


01:11:36.206 --> 01:11:38.174
Oh, my God. ls he okay?


01:11:38.542 --> 01:11:40.510
He's fine. Not injured at all.


01:11:41.478 --> 01:11:42.945
l'm sorry, my friend.


01:11:43.113 --> 01:11:44.842
-What happened?
-We drank, we fought,


01:11:44.982 --> 01:11:46.449
he made his ancestors proud.


01:11:46.950 --> 01:11:48.747
Put him on the bed.


01:11:59.997 --> 01:12:03.524
l still don't think
you're the God of Thunder.


01:12:04.234 --> 01:12:06.361
But you ought to be.


01:12:17.514 --> 01:12:18.981
Are these your chambers?


01:12:19.416 --> 01:12:23.045
lt's more of a temporary living situation.


01:12:23.921 --> 01:12:27.721
l'm sorry. l don't usually have guests.


01:12:28.425 --> 01:12:31.223
Actually, l never have guests.


01:12:33.430 --> 01:12:35.557
That's not the right place for it.


01:12:36.600 --> 01:12:38.227
l'm sorry.


01:12:41.371 --> 01:12:42.360
Can we go outside?


01:12:43.273 --> 01:12:44.672
Yes, of course.


01:12:50.213 --> 01:12:52.477
l come up here sometimes
when l can't sleep


01:12:52.583 --> 01:12:56.679
or l'm trying to reconcile particle data,
or when Darcy's driving me crazy.


01:12:57.955 --> 01:13:01.254
l come up here a lot, actually,
now that l think about it.


01:13:05.295 --> 01:13:07.195
l'm really glad you're safe.


01:13:08.298 --> 01:13:10.766
You've been very kind to me,


01:13:11.535 --> 01:13:13.696
and l've been far less grateful
than you deserve.


01:13:13.904 --> 01:13:15.565
Well, l hit you with my car
a couple times,


01:13:15.706 --> 01:13:17.697
so l think that kind of evens things out.


01:13:20.143 --> 01:13:21.940
Perhaps l had it coming.


01:13:27.818 --> 01:13:29.115
Oh, my God!


01:13:30.420 --> 01:13:31.717
l don't believe it!


01:13:31.989 --> 01:13:35.390
lt was all l could get back.
l'm sorry it's not as much as l promised.


01:13:35.492 --> 01:13:40.122
No, no, this is great! This is...
l don't have to start from scratch now.


01:13:40.497 --> 01:13:41.794
Thank you.


01:13:46.503 --> 01:13:47.902
What's wrong?


01:13:49.339 --> 01:13:50.306
S.H.l.E.L.D.


01:13:50.440 --> 01:13:51.737
Whatever they are,


01:13:53.276 --> 01:13:54.868
they're gonna do
everything in their power


01:13:54.978 --> 01:13:57.640
to make sure this research
never sees the light of day.


01:13:57.848 --> 01:13:59.145
No, Jane.


01:13:59.783 --> 01:14:01.648
Listen to me. You must not give up.


01:14:01.952 --> 01:14:03.920
-You must finish what you've started.
-Why?


01:14:04.187 --> 01:14:05.745
Because you're right.


01:14:06.289 --> 01:14:07.586
Here, look.


01:14:10.193 --> 01:14:13.651
Your ancestors called it magic,
and you call it science.


01:14:14.297 --> 01:14:16.993
Well, l come from a place
where they're one and the same thing.


01:14:31.648 --> 01:14:33.172
What is that?


01:14:34.217 --> 01:14:37.311
My father explained it to me like this,


01:14:37.454 --> 01:14:39.149
that your world


01:14:39.289 --> 01:14:42.087
is one of the Nine Realms
of the Cosmos,


01:14:42.192 --> 01:14:45.161
linked to each other
by the branches of Yggdrasil,


01:14:45.562 --> 01:14:47.462
the Worlds Tree.


01:14:47.731 --> 01:14:50.359
Now you see it every day
without realizing.


01:14:50.734 --> 01:14:53.703
The images glimpsed through...
What did you call it?


01:14:54.237 --> 01:14:55.966
This Hooble Telescope.


01:14:56.573 --> 01:14:59.371
-Hubble.
-Hubble Telescope.


01:15:02.512 --> 01:15:03.809
Tell me more.


01:15:04.414 --> 01:15:05.881
So, the Nine Realms.


01:15:06.583 --> 01:15:09.051
Now, there is Midgard, which is Earth.


01:15:09.419 --> 01:15:10.886
This is Alfheim.


01:15:11.254 --> 01:15:13.882
Vanaheim. Jotunheim.


01:15:14.758 --> 01:15:16.055
And Asgard.


01:15:16.593 --> 01:15:18.493
<i>And that's where l come from.</i>


01:15:35.946 --> 01:15:37.243
Thank you, Jane.


01:15:40.717 --> 01:15:43.652
Our dearest friend banished,
Loki on the throne,


01:15:43.754 --> 01:15:47.087
Asgard on the brink of war,
yet you've managed to consume


01:15:47.290 --> 01:15:50.350
four wild boar,
six pheasant, a side of beef,


01:15:50.460 --> 01:15:53.896
and two casks of ale. Shame on you.
Don't you care?


01:15:54.731 --> 01:15:56.756
Do not mistake my appetite for apathy!


01:15:57.067 --> 01:15:58.864
Stop it, both of you!


01:15:59.236 --> 01:16:00.203
Stop.


01:16:01.571 --> 01:16:03.937
-We all know what we have to do.
-We must go.


01:16:06.576 --> 01:16:08.874
We must find Thor.


01:16:10.080 --> 01:16:11.047
lt's treason.


01:16:11.314 --> 01:16:13.043
To hell with treason, it's suicide.


01:16:13.316 --> 01:16:15.284
Thor would do the same for us.


01:16:16.419 --> 01:16:17.716
Now shush.


01:16:19.322 --> 01:16:21.552
Heimdall might be watching.


01:16:26.596 --> 01:16:29.224
Heimdall demands your presence.


01:16:33.770 --> 01:16:35.067
We're doomed.


01:16:35.338 --> 01:16:38.796
You would defy the commands of Loki,
our king,


01:16:39.509 --> 01:16:41.909
break every oath you
have taken as warriors,


01:16:42.012 --> 01:16:44.310
and commit treason to bring Thor back?


01:16:44.514 --> 01:16:45.981
-Yes.
-Good.


01:16:46.616 --> 01:16:47.640
So you'll help us?


01:16:47.851 --> 01:16:52.618
l am bound by honor to our king.
l cannot open the bridge to you.


01:16:53.356 --> 01:16:54.983
Complicated fellow, isn't he?


01:16:55.292 --> 01:16:56.919
Now what do we do?


01:16:58.361 --> 01:16:59.589
Look!


01:17:19.015 --> 01:17:20.312
-What the hell was that?
-l don't know, sir.


01:17:20.450 --> 01:17:21.678
We got massive energy readings
out of nowhere


01:17:21.818 --> 01:17:24.286
and then they just disappeared.
Fifteen miles due northwest.


01:17:24.387 --> 01:17:25.684
Let's go take a look.


01:17:50.714 --> 01:17:51.942
Thank you.


01:17:52.048 --> 01:17:54.016
-Thank you.
-You're very welcome.


01:18:01.191 --> 01:18:03.989
<i>Base to Team 2,</i>
<i>we've got activity outside the town.</i>


01:18:04.094 --> 01:18:05.186
<i>Stay on your target.</i>


01:18:14.571 --> 01:18:17.039
Ensure my brother does not return.


01:18:20.911 --> 01:18:22.538
Destroy everything.


01:18:33.423 --> 01:18:34.720
Mom?


01:18:42.632 --> 01:18:44.600
ls there a Renaissance Fair in town?


01:18:44.734 --> 01:18:46.031
Call it in.


01:18:46.736 --> 01:18:47.703
Yeah.


01:18:49.639 --> 01:18:53.200
Base, we've got Xena, Jackie Chan
and Robin Hood.


01:18:53.810 --> 01:18:56.040
lt's a beautiful theory, Jane.


01:18:56.813 --> 01:19:00.044
But you won't be able to convince
the scientific community of any of it.


01:19:00.150 --> 01:19:01.447
Not without hard evidence.


01:19:02.419 --> 01:19:03.386
Found you!


01:19:09.759 --> 01:19:11.386
My friends!


01:19:12.896 --> 01:19:14.887
This is good! This is good.


01:19:15.298 --> 01:19:16.458
l don't believe it.


01:19:16.967 --> 01:19:19.595
Excuse me.
Lady Sif and the Warriors Three.


01:19:22.405 --> 01:19:23.895
My friends,


01:19:24.007 --> 01:19:26.475
l've never been happier to see anyone.


01:19:26.910 --> 01:19:28.377
But you should not have come.


01:19:30.480 --> 01:19:31.640
We're here to take you home.


01:19:33.249 --> 01:19:34.807
You know l can't go home.


01:19:37.253 --> 01:19:38.743
My father


01:19:39.823 --> 01:19:40.915
is dead because of me.


01:19:41.925 --> 01:19:44.120
And l must remain in exile.


01:19:44.260 --> 01:19:45.420
Thor,


01:19:45.862 --> 01:19:47.454
your father still lives.


01:20:02.879 --> 01:20:05.814
Tell me, Loki,
how did you get the Jotuns into Asgard?


01:20:06.316 --> 01:20:09.513
You think the Bifrost is the only way
in and out of this realm?


01:20:09.652 --> 01:20:11.142
There are secret paths
between the worlds


01:20:11.287 --> 01:20:13.949
to which even you, with all your gifts,
are blind.


01:20:14.057 --> 01:20:17.185
But l have need of them no longer,
now that l am king.


01:20:17.327 --> 01:20:18.954
And l say, for your act of treason,


01:20:19.295 --> 01:20:21.957
you are relieved of your duties
as Gatekeeper,


01:20:22.132 --> 01:20:23.827
and no longer citizen of Asgard.


01:20:24.334 --> 01:20:26.928
Then l need no longer obey you.


01:20:47.490 --> 01:20:50.323
Get somebody from Linguistics
down here.


01:21:17.687 --> 01:21:19.382
Was somebody else coming?


01:21:23.593 --> 01:21:24.582
ls that one of Stark's?


01:21:24.727 --> 01:21:28.254
l don't know.
The guy never tells me anything.


01:21:32.035 --> 01:21:33.229
<i>Hello.</i>


01:21:33.369 --> 01:21:36.031
<i>You are using</i>
<i>unregistered weapons technology.</i>


01:21:36.139 --> 01:21:37.265
<i>ldentify yourself.</i>


01:21:41.077 --> 01:21:42.044
Here we go.


01:21:45.648 --> 01:21:46.774
lncoming!


01:21:54.557 --> 01:21:55.854
Jane, you have to leave.


01:21:55.992 --> 01:21:57.960
-What are you gonna do?
-l'm staying here.


01:21:58.261 --> 01:21:59.888
Thor's going to fight with us!


01:22:00.263 --> 01:22:01.560
My friends,


01:22:01.998 --> 01:22:05.957
l'm just a man. l'll only be in the way,
or worse, get one of you killed.


01:22:06.102 --> 01:22:08.127
But l can help
get these people to safety.


01:22:08.438 --> 01:22:10.463
Well, if you're staying, then so am l.


01:22:10.773 --> 01:22:13.071
-We'll need some time.
-You'll have it!


01:22:13.743 --> 01:22:15.210
Okay, move it, people!


01:22:16.112 --> 01:22:18.239
Everybody out! Use the back door.


01:22:18.915 --> 01:22:20.246
Go, hurry! You can eat later.


01:22:32.962 --> 01:22:34.827
Keep it distracted.


01:22:49.512 --> 01:22:51.946
For Asgard!


01:23:27.350 --> 01:23:28.317
Fall back!


01:23:45.034 --> 01:23:46.023
Go. Now. Run!


01:24:14.364 --> 01:24:16.832
Sif. Sif, you've done all you can.


01:24:17.200 --> 01:24:19.395
No. l will die a warrior's death.


01:24:19.702 --> 01:24:21.602
Stories will be told of this day.


01:24:21.904 --> 01:24:24.600
Live, and tell those stories yourself.


01:24:27.210 --> 01:24:28.734
Now go.


01:24:36.252 --> 01:24:39.187
You must return to Asgard.
You have to stop Loki.


01:24:39.455 --> 01:24:40.854
What about you?


01:24:40.957 --> 01:24:43.425
Do not worry, my friends. l have a plan.


01:24:44.227 --> 01:24:45.353
Come on.


01:24:49.432 --> 01:24:51.730
We need to fall back. Come on.


01:24:51.834 --> 01:24:52.801
Come on.


01:25:00.743 --> 01:25:01.869
Wait!


01:25:09.819 --> 01:25:10.945
What's he doing?


01:25:37.814 --> 01:25:41.477
Brother,
whatever l have done to wrong you,


01:25:41.851 --> 01:25:44.820
whatever l have done
to lead you to do this,


01:25:45.188 --> 01:25:46.985
l am truly sorry.


01:25:47.724 --> 01:25:50.192
<i>But these people are innocent.</i>


01:25:51.361 --> 01:25:54.660
Taking their lives will gain you nothing.


01:26:02.205 --> 01:26:03.672
So take mine


01:26:04.474 --> 01:26:05.702
and end this.


01:26:19.822 --> 01:26:20.789
No.


01:26:36.906 --> 01:26:38.203
lt's over.


01:26:38.574 --> 01:26:40.872
No. lt's not over.


01:26:41.511 --> 01:26:43.411
l mean, you're safe.


01:26:43.746 --> 01:26:45.509
We're safe.


01:26:45.915 --> 01:26:47.212
lt's over.


01:26:53.256 --> 01:26:54.484
No.


01:27:12.909 --> 01:27:13.933
No.


01:27:39.836 --> 01:27:41.963
-We're spiking.
-Levels increase!


01:27:42.305 --> 01:27:43.932
Whosoever holds this hammer,


01:27:46.509 --> 01:27:47.476
if he be worthy,


01:27:50.913 --> 01:27:52.642
shall possess the power of Thor.


01:28:08.598 --> 01:28:09.565
Jane!


01:28:12.101 --> 01:28:15.093
-No. No. No!
-Come!


01:28:35.992 --> 01:28:39.519
Oh. My. God.


01:29:49.031 --> 01:29:50.362
So, is this how you normally look?


01:29:51.267 --> 01:29:52.234
More or less.


01:29:53.202 --> 01:29:54.829
lt's a good look.


01:29:55.371 --> 01:29:58.397
We must go to the Bifrost site.
l would have words with my brother.


01:29:58.541 --> 01:29:59.565
Excuse me!


01:30:03.546 --> 01:30:04.843
Donald?


01:30:05.948 --> 01:30:07.381
l don't think
you've been completely honest with me.


01:30:07.483 --> 01:30:08.677
Know this, Son of Coul.


01:30:08.951 --> 01:30:11.920
You and l, we fight for the same cause,
the protection of this world.


01:30:12.054 --> 01:30:14.045
From this day forward,
you can count me as your ally


01:30:14.156 --> 01:30:17.125
if you return the items
you have taken from Jane.


01:30:17.259 --> 01:30:18.886
-Stolen.
-Borrowed.


01:30:19.795 --> 01:30:21.888
Of course,
you can have your equipment back.


01:30:21.998 --> 01:30:24.125
You're gonna need it
to continue your research.


01:30:24.967 --> 01:30:27.231
Would you like to see
the bridge we spoke of?


01:30:28.437 --> 01:30:29.529
Sure.


01:30:31.240 --> 01:30:33.208
Wait, l need to debrief you!


01:30:40.449 --> 01:30:41.609
Welcome to Asgard.


01:31:07.309 --> 01:31:09.436
Heimdall, open the Bifrost.


01:31:17.186 --> 01:31:18.448
Heimdall?


01:31:22.692 --> 01:31:23.989
<i>Heimdall!</i>


01:31:26.162 --> 01:31:27.527
He doesn't answer.


01:31:28.297 --> 01:31:29.787
Then we are stranded.


01:31:29.899 --> 01:31:32.800
Heimdall!
lf you can hear me, we need you now!


01:31:33.736 --> 01:31:36.466
<i>Heimdall! We need you now!</i>


01:31:42.912 --> 01:31:44.174
Heimdall!


01:31:58.761 --> 01:32:01.855
l must go back to Asgard,
but l give you my word,


01:32:03.099 --> 01:32:05.397
l will return for you.


01:32:13.042 --> 01:32:14.202
Deal?


01:32:27.790 --> 01:32:29.087
Deal.


01:32:45.541 --> 01:32:47.600
Get him to the healing room!


01:32:49.078 --> 01:32:50.602
Leave my brother to me.


01:33:15.504 --> 01:33:16.971
lt's said


01:33:17.339 --> 01:33:21.969
you can still hear and see
what transpires around you.


01:33:23.345 --> 01:33:25.472
l hope it's true,


01:33:27.349 --> 01:33:29.476
so that you may know


01:33:30.519 --> 01:33:34.455
your death came at the hand


01:33:35.357 --> 01:33:36.654
of Laufey.


01:33:45.801 --> 01:33:48.292
And your death came
by the son of Odin.


01:33:54.210 --> 01:33:55.575
Loki!


01:33:55.678 --> 01:33:57.145
You saved him!


01:34:01.650 --> 01:34:03.914
l swear to you, Mother,


01:34:04.019 --> 01:34:06.453
that they will pay for what
they've done today.


01:34:06.856 --> 01:34:07.845
Loki.


01:34:08.657 --> 01:34:09.681
Thor!


01:34:10.726 --> 01:34:12.626
l knew you'd return to us.


01:34:18.234 --> 01:34:19.667
Why don't you tell her


01:34:19.902 --> 01:34:23.360
how you sent the Destroyer
to kill our friends, to kill me?


01:34:23.505 --> 01:34:24.472
What?


01:34:24.573 --> 01:34:26.973
Why, it must have been enforcing
Father's last command.


01:34:27.076 --> 01:34:29.943
You're a talented liar, Brother.
Always have been.


01:34:30.579 --> 01:34:31.807
lt's good to have you back.


01:34:32.248 --> 01:34:35.809
Now if you'll excuse me,
l have to destroy Jotunheim.


01:35:17.426 --> 01:35:18.723
You can't stop it.


01:35:18.861 --> 01:35:22.160
The Bifrost will build until
it rips Jotunheim apart.


01:35:44.053 --> 01:35:45.179
Jane?


01:35:47.156 --> 01:35:48.623
Why have you done this?


01:35:48.924 --> 01:35:52.621
To prove to Father
that l am the worthy son.


01:35:52.761 --> 01:35:55.559
When he wakes,
l will have saved his life.


01:35:55.664 --> 01:35:58.360
l will have destroyed that
race of monsters.


01:35:58.467 --> 01:36:00.560
And l will be true heir to the throne!


01:36:00.970 --> 01:36:02.938
You can't kill an entire race!


01:36:03.072 --> 01:36:04.369
Why not?


01:36:07.176 --> 01:36:10.407
And what is this newfound love
for the Frost Giants?


01:36:11.447 --> 01:36:14.814
You could have killed them all
with your bare hands.


01:36:14.984 --> 01:36:16.975
-l've changed.
-So have l.


01:36:18.787 --> 01:36:20.254
Now fight me.


01:36:23.192 --> 01:36:25.092
l never wanted the throne!


01:36:26.462 --> 01:36:28.259
l only ever wanted to be your equal.


01:36:29.131 --> 01:36:31.099
l will not fight you, Brother!


01:36:31.200 --> 01:36:32.599
l'm not your brother.


01:36:33.369 --> 01:36:34.631
l never was.


01:36:34.770 --> 01:36:36.237
Loki, this is madness.


01:36:36.839 --> 01:36:38.431
ls it madness?


01:36:39.308 --> 01:36:40.434
ls it?


01:36:41.877 --> 01:36:43.105
ls it?


01:36:44.213 --> 01:36:48.172
Come on. What happened to you
on Earth that turned you so soft?


01:36:49.018 --> 01:36:51.680
Don't tell me it was that woman.


01:36:53.722 --> 01:36:54.916
lt was!


01:36:55.024 --> 01:36:59.120
Well, maybe, when we're finished here,
l'll pay her a visit myself!


01:37:41.503 --> 01:37:43.368
Thor!


01:37:50.179 --> 01:37:51.646
Brother, please.


01:38:03.192 --> 01:38:04.318
Enough!


01:38:48.137 --> 01:38:49.263
Look at you,


01:38:51.974 --> 01:38:53.271
the Mighty Thor,


01:38:56.411 --> 01:38:58.538
with all your strength,


01:38:59.248 --> 01:39:01.876
and what good does it do you now?


01:39:03.252 --> 01:39:06.983
Do you hear me, Brother?
There's nothing you can do!


01:39:25.007 --> 01:39:26.269
What are you doing?


01:39:28.010 --> 01:39:31.343
lf you destroy the bridge,
you'll never see her again!


01:39:41.023 --> 01:39:42.650
Forgive me, Jane.


01:40:21.196 --> 01:40:23.164
l could have done it, Father!


01:40:24.199 --> 01:40:25.996
l could have done it!


01:40:26.435 --> 01:40:27.732
For you!


01:40:28.503 --> 01:40:29.970
For all of us!


01:40:32.174 --> 01:40:33.471
No, Loki.


01:40:42.251 --> 01:40:43.218
Loki, no.


01:40:44.519 --> 01:40:46.646
No!


01:40:50.926 --> 01:40:52.052
No.


01:41:08.443 --> 01:41:09.740
lt's gone.


01:42:22.317 --> 01:42:25.115
And then, with a mighty bellow,


01:42:25.387 --> 01:42:29.448
l flew into the giant metal creature
and laid him low!


01:42:29.658 --> 01:42:33.185
ls that another way of saying
you fell on your huge ass?


01:42:33.328 --> 01:42:39.289
As a matter of fact, falling was a tactic
lulling the Destroyer...


01:42:53.515 --> 01:42:56.313
My Queen, l'm so sorry for your loss.


01:43:02.190 --> 01:43:03.487
<i>How is he?</i>


01:43:05.861 --> 01:43:07.829
<i>He mourns for his brother.</i>


01:43:09.197 --> 01:43:10.323
<i>And...</i>


01:43:11.533 --> 01:43:13.057
<i>He misses her.</i>


01:43:14.102 --> 01:43:15.399
<i>The mortal.</i>


01:43:31.887 --> 01:43:33.582
You'll be a wise king.


01:43:38.059 --> 01:43:40.425
There will never be
a wiser king than you.


01:43:41.897 --> 01:43:43.524
Or a better father.


01:43:54.443 --> 01:43:57.571
l have much to learn.


01:43:59.614 --> 01:44:01.081
l know that now.


01:44:06.121 --> 01:44:08.055
Someday, perhaps,


01:44:09.391 --> 01:44:11.256
l shall make you proud.


01:44:18.934 --> 01:44:21.095
You've already made me proud.


01:44:35.684 --> 01:44:37.652
So Earth is lost to us.


01:44:39.020 --> 01:44:39.987
No.


01:44:41.022 --> 01:44:42.990
There is always hope.


01:44:47.028 --> 01:44:48.495
Can you see her?


01:44:51.466 --> 01:44:52.763
<i>Yes.</i>


01:44:56.471 --> 01:44:58.336
l have the particle detectors!


01:44:58.473 --> 01:45:00.498
Darcy, do you have the S.H.l.E.L.D.
satellite codes?


01:45:00.642 --> 01:45:02.667
Yeah. Have you seen my taser?


01:45:02.811 --> 01:45:04.176
<i>How is she?</i>


01:45:04.312 --> 01:45:06.337
ln the car. Come on, Jane!


01:45:06.715 --> 01:45:08.774
<i>She searches for you.</i>


01:53:18.373 --> 01:53:20.273
Dr. Selvig.


01:53:23.144 --> 01:53:25.271
So you're the man behind all this?


01:53:27.482 --> 01:53:29.450
lt's quite a labyrinth.


01:53:30.218 --> 01:53:34.120
l was thinking
they're taking me down here to kill me.


01:53:41.329 --> 01:53:44.298
l've been hearing
about the New Mexico situation.


01:53:45.166 --> 01:53:48.795
Your work has impressed a lot of people
who are much smarter than l am.


01:53:48.903 --> 01:53:50.871
l have a lot to work with.


01:53:51.506 --> 01:53:54.771
The Foster Theory.
A gateway to another dimension.


01:53:55.476 --> 01:53:56.443
lt's unprecedented.


01:53:59.180 --> 01:54:00.374
lsn't it?


01:54:03.851 --> 01:54:07.150
Legend tells us one thing,
history, another.


01:54:07.522 --> 01:54:11.686
But every now and then,
we find something that belongs to both.


01:54:19.534 --> 01:54:20.501
What is it?


01:54:20.601 --> 01:54:21.693
Power, Doctor.


01:54:22.270 --> 01:54:24.238
lf we can figure out how to tap it,


01:54:24.705 --> 01:54:26.172
maybe unlimited power.


01:54:31.946 --> 01:54:34.176
Well, l guess that's worth a look.


01:54:35.950 --> 01:54:38.180
Well, l guess that's worth a look.

